Screens is a simple utility to grab a random "screen" from the directorygiven by $HOME/.screens and put it on the terminal screen.  Normally, it'san ascii file, but if you have files in that directory that end in ".g",and have a terminal with Zenith emulation, it will display that file inZenith graphics mode.  Naturally, you can always put the graphics escapecodes for whatever terminal in your file.Any bug reports go to russ@uokmax.UUCP or texsun!uokmax!russ.  Thanks.